    "result_text": "I fixed `mock_openai()` in `tests/fakes.py`, and both digest tests pass again with `pytest -q`. One cleanup step is left for you: I couldn't delete my throwaway check file `tests/test_tmp_check.py` because removing it needed approval. Please delete it.\n\n**Cause:** openai 3.19.2 no longer sends requests through `httpx`. It uses `httpx2` and `httpcore2` instead. respx 0.23.1 only intercepts `httpx` and `httpcore`, so it never saw the OpenAI requests. Its router simply matched nothing, which is why there was no warning.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **Interception:** while the `with` block is open, `mock_openai()` replaces `httpx2.HTTPTransport.handle_request` at the class level, using `unittest.mock.patch.object`. Because the patch is on the class, it covers every OpenAI client whatever its creation time: `app.digest`'s cached client, clients created before the block and clients created inside it. The patch is removed when the block exits.\n- **Replies:** `POST \u2026/v1/chat/completions` gets the canned replies in order, and a request beyond them gets a 400. The yielded list of request bodies works as before.\n- **Other requests:** any other request made through `httpx2`'s default transport inside the block raises an `AssertionError` rather than reaching the network. This matches how respx blocked unmatched requests before.\n- **Guard:** if a future openai release stops using `httpx2`, the helper raises a clear `RuntimeError` instead of silently missing requests.\n- **Interface:** the helper's signature and behaviour are unchanged. `tests/fakes.py` no longer imports `respx` or `httpx`. Nothing in `app/`, `pyproject.toml` or the pytest config changed.\n\n**Check:** the throwaway test confirmed that a client created before the block and one created inside it both get the canned replies. It also confirmed that the extra request gets the 400, and that a request after the block goes to the real network. That last request is what produced the expected pytest-socket warning in that run.\n\nSince the modu"
